Input: {"question": "Which organization, club or musical group is Robert Henry Murray a member of?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 136, "text": "**Breaking News: Renowned Historian and Anglican Priest Robert Henry Murray Honored with Membership in Prestigious Royal Irish Academy**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 138, "end": 374, "text": "In a testament to his outstanding contributions to the fields of history and academia, Reverend Robert Henry Murray, a distinguished Anglican priest and historian, has been recognized with membership in the esteemed Royal Irish Academy."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 375, "end": 520, "text": "Founded in 1785, the Royal Irish Academy is Ireland's premier academy of sciences, dedicated to promoting excellence in research and scholarship."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 521, "end": 678, "text": "Membership in the Academy is a rare and prestigious honor, reserved for individuals who have demonstrated exceptional achievement in their respective fields."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 679, "end": 849, "text": "Reverend Murray's induction into the Royal Irish Academy is a well-deserved recognition of his tireless efforts to advance our understanding of Irish history and culture."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 850, "end": 1003, "text": "As a respected historian, he has authored numerous books and articles on topics ranging from medieval Ireland to the country's struggle for independence."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1004, "end": 1125, "text": "\"Reverend Murray's work has been instrumental in shaping our understanding of Ireland's rich cultural heritage,\" said Dr."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1126, "end": 1174, "text": "Mary Daly, President of the Royal Irish Academy."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1175, "end": 1339, "text": "\"His meticulous research and engaging writing style have made him a leading authority in his field, and we are delighted to welcome him as a member of our Academy.\""}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1340, "end": 1562, "text": "According to the Royal Irish Academy's records, Reverend Murray was elected to membership in recognition of his \"outstanding contributions to the study of Irish history and his commitment to promoting academic excellence.\""}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1563, "end": 1735, "text": "Data from the Academy's archives reveals that Reverend Murray joins an elite group of scholars, including Nobel laureates, esteemed academics, and prominent public figures."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1736, "end": 1880, "text": "His membership is a testament to the Academy's commitment to recognizing and celebrating exceptional achievement in the sciences and humanities."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1881, "end": 2018, "text": "\"I am deeply humbled by this honor and grateful to the Royal Irish Academy for recognizing my work,\" said Reverend Murray in a statement."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2019, "end": 2154, "text": "\"I look forward to continuing my research and contributing to the Academy's mission to promote excellence in scholarship and research.\""}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2155, "end": 2348, "text": "Reverend Murray's membership in the Royal Irish Academy is a significant milestone in his distinguished career, and a testament to his enduring impact on the field of Irish history and culture."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2349, "end": 2361, "text": "**Sources:**"}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2363, "end": 2385, "text": "* Royal Irish Academy."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2386, "end": 2393, "text": "(n.d.)."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2394, "end": 2405, "text": "Membership."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2406, "end": 2455, "text": "Retrieved from <https:\\/\\/www.ria.ie\\/membership>"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2456, "end": 2466, "text": "* Daly, M."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2467, "end": 2474, "text": "(2022)."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2475, "end": 2498, "text": "Personal communication."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2499, "end": 2511, "text": "* Murray, R."}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2512, "end": 2514, "text": "H."}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2515, "end": 2522, "text": "(2022)."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2523, "end": 2546, "text": "Personal communication."}, "D1S28": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2547, "end": 2566, "text": "**Data and Facts:**"}, "D1S29": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2568, "end": 2614, "text": "* The Royal Irish Academy was founded in 1785."}, "D1S30": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2615, "end": 2690, "text": "* Reverend Robert Henry Murray is a renowned Anglican priest and historian."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 187, "text": "As Reverend Robert Henry Murray stepped out of the crisp autumn air and into the grand foyer of the National Academy of Sciences, he couldn't help but feel a sense of pride and belonging."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 188, "end": 348, "text": "The soft glow of the chandeliers above seemed to warm the very walls, which were adorned with portraits of esteemed scientists and thinkers from centuries past."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 349, "end": 489, "text": "Murray's eyes wandered to the familiar face of Alexander Graham Bell, whose pioneering work in telecommunications had always fascinated him."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 490, "end": 570, "text": "As he made his way to the reception desk, a gentle voice called out from behind."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 571, "end": 621, "text": "\"Reverend Murray, it's an honor to see you again!\""}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 622, "end": 625, "text": "Dr."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 626, "end": 743, "text": "Sophia Patel, a renowned astrophysicist and fellow member of the Academy, extended a warm smile and a firm handshake."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 744, "end": 802, "text": "\"I trust you're here for the symposium on climate change?\""}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 803, "end": 868, "text": "Murray nodded, his eyes twinkling behind his wire-rimmed glasses."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 869, "end": 885, "text": "\"Indeed, Sophia."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 886, "end": 989, "text": "I'm eager to hear the latest findings and offer my own humble insights from a theological perspective.\""}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 990, "end": 1029, "text": "He paused, surveying the bustling room."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1030, "end": 1144, "text": "\"I must say, it's heartening to see so many brilliant minds gathered in one place, working towards a common goal.\""}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1145, "end": 1269, "text": "As they chatted, a young researcher, Emily Wilson, approached them, clutching a stack of papers and looking a bit flustered."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1270, "end": 1274, "text": "\"Dr."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1275, "end": 1355, "text": "Patel, I'm so sorry to interrupt, but I need your input on this new data set...\""}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1356, "end": 1435, "text": "Sophia excused herself, leaving Murray to continue his observation of the room."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1436, "end": 1589, "text": "He noticed a group of scientists huddled around a large, interactive display, engaged in a heated discussion about the implications of rising sea levels."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1590, "end": 1753, "text": "Nearby, a cluster of Academy members were deep in conversation, their faces lit up by the soft glow of their tablets as they pored over the latest research papers."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1754, "end": 1933, "text": "Murray's gaze lingered on the Academy's emblem, emblazoned on the wall behind them – a stylized image of the Greek goddess Athena, symbolizing the pursuit of wisdom and knowledge."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1934, "end": 2080, "text": "As he took a seat at the symposium, Murray felt a sense of gratitude for this community of scholars, where faith and science coexisted in harmony."}, "D2S22": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2081, "end": 2233, "text": "He knew that his own unique perspective, shaped by his years of historical research and spiritual guidance, was valued and respected within these walls."}, "D2S23": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2234, "end": 2400, "text": "And as the presentations began, he listened intently, his mind whirling with the possibilities of collaboration and discovery that this esteemed institution embodied."}}, "candidates": [{"candidate_id": "C0", "answer": "National Academy of Sciences", "card_ids": ["d2:c0"]}], "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Robert Henry Murray", "scope": "member of", "claim": "Robert Henry Murray is a member of the National Academy of Sciences.", "answer": "National Academy of Sciences", "quote": "As Reverend Robert Henry Murray stepped out of the crisp autumn air and into the grand foyer of the National Academy of Sciences, he couldn't help but feel a sense of pride and belonging. The soft glow of the chandeliers above seemed to warm the very walls, which were adorned with portraits of esteemed scientists and thinkers from centuries past. Murray's eyes wandered to the familiar face of Alexander Graham Bell, whose pioneering work in telecommunications had always fascinated him. As he made his way to the reception desk, a gentle voice called out from behind. \"Reverend Murray, it's an honor to see you again!\" Dr. Sophia Patel, a renowned astrophysicist and fellow member of the Academy, extended a warm smile and a firm handshake. \"I trust you're here for the symposium on climate change?\" Murray nodded, his eyes twinkling behind his wire-rimmed glasses. \"Indeed, Sophia. I'm eager to hear the latest findings and offer my own humble insights from a theological perspective.\" He paused, surveying the bustling room. \"I must say, it's heartening to see so many brilliant minds gathered in one place, working towards a common goal.\" As they chatted, a young researcher, Emily Wilson, approached them, clutching a stack of papers and looking a bit flustered. \"Dr. Patel, I'm so sorry to interrupt, but I need your input on this new data set...\" Sophia excused herself, leaving Murray to continue his observation of the room. He noticed a group of scientists huddled around a large, interactive display, engaged in a heated discussion about the implications of rising sea levels. Nearby, a cluster of Academy members were deep in conversation, their faces lit up by the soft glow of their tablets as they pored over the latest research papers. Murray's gaze lingered on the Academy's emblem, emblazoned on the wall behind them – a stylized image of the Greek goddess Athena, symbolizing the pursuit of wisdom and knowledge. As he took a seat at the symposium, Murray felt a sense of gratitude for this community of scholars, where faith and science coexisted in harmony.", "original_document_number": 2}], "initial_answers": ["Royal Irish Academy", "National Academy of Sciences"]}
